      "text": [
        " الرَّجُلِ يُصَلِّي الصَّلَاةَ وَحْدَهُ ثُمَّ يَجِدُ جَمَاعَةً قَالَ يُصَلِّي مَعَهُمْ وَ يَجْعَلُهَا الْفَرِيضَةَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin Shazaan, and Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, altogether from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hafs Bin Al Bakhtary, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the man who prays the <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> alone, then he finds a <span class=\"iTxt\">Jam’at</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He should pray <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> with them, and he should make it to be an Oblligatory (<span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn ’Isma’il has narrated from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan and Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from all from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hafs ibn al-Bakhtariy who has said the following: “I once asked abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who performs Salah (prayer) alone then finds a congregation. He (the Imam) said, ’He can perform Salah (prayer) with them and make it to be an obligatory one.”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
